1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Roll the mouse wheel back and forth to search for the map in the 3D window.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Press the mouse button and move the mouse to scale.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The scale will maintain the original map search and angle.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Press the mouse button and move the mouse to rotate to check the details.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Press the button in the 3D window to rotate and adjust the engagement position.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
The function is called focus.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Press the mouse button and move the mouse to the preview view in the menu.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Or press the number button to change the view.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Press the mouse button and move the mouse to change the view.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Similarly, in the 2D window, rotate the mouse wheel to zoom in and out.

11
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:13,000
The difference is that the 2D window will be zoomed in and out with the mouse pointer as the center.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The center of the mouse and the movement of the mouse can be parallel.

13
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
In addition, you can change the speed control settings in the user settings.

14
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
It is up to you to choose other 3D software settings or change specific settings.

